---
import FeaturesLayout from '../../layouts/FeaturesLayout.astro';
const inlineCode = 'text-cdx-text bg-cdx-bg-alt rounded px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.85em]';
---

<FeaturesLayout
  currentSlug="tips"
  title="Tips and Tricks — compodocx"
  description="Patterns that pay off in real-world compodocx setups: monorepo layout, watch + serve, CI diffs, narrow doc tsconfigs, and Pagefind tuning."
>
  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary text-lg">
    Patterns that pay off in real projects. None of these are required — they&rsquo;re what we reach
    for when the basics are in place.
  </p>

  <ul class="text-cdx-text-secondary space-y-4 text-sm">
    <li>
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">Monorepos.</strong>
      One compodocx run per project, <code class={inlineCode}>--basePath</code> each into a shared
      <code class={inlineCode}>/docs</code> folder, link from a static index. Each project keeps its own
      version-switcher and theme.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">Watch + serve.</strong>
      <code class={inlineCode}>--watch --serve</code> gives you instant feedback while authoring. The
      dev server reuses the same routing and search index as production — what you see locally matches
      what ships.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">CI diffs against the last release.</strong>
      Run <code class={inlineCode}>compodocx diff --against last-tag</code> in CI to compute API deltas.
      Pipe the JSON to your bot of choice for PR comments. Breaking changes exit non-zero.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">Heavy generic types render slower.</strong>
      Keep your doc tsconfig narrow — exclude test files, storybook, dev-only entries. The smaller the
      surface, the faster the build.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">Pagefind index for very large repos.</strong>
      Built automatically. For repos over ~5k symbols, set
      <code class={inlineCode}>--searchIndex=false</code> to skip and rely on Cmd+K&rsquo;s built-in fuzzy
      match instead — saves ~10 s per build.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">Preserve comments through the build.</strong>
      Some bundlers strip JSDoc by default. Set
      <code class={inlineCode}>"removeComments": false</code> in your doc tsconfig if you see empty descriptions.
    </li>
  </ul>
</FeaturesLayout>
